From 0b35251bcd7adeed4f300bd70e1462edbb52cd7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: danilo neves cruz <cruzdanilo@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 21:35:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: avoid redundant delays in web viewport reads

hierarchy lookups read the viewport width and height before querying the
dom, paying two unrelated 100 ms delays. read those dimensions immediately
and retain the existing delay for hierarchy queries, css queries and actions.
this preserves the ten-attempt hierarchy recovery window and prevents
unsuccessful element searches from traversing the dom without a gap.

move the removed 200 ms into settling samples, keeping their aggregate
300 ms delay and the existing 200 ms delay after a hierarchy change. other
drivers retain their timing. viewport dimensions remain live across resizes.

cover recovery, polling and settling with deterministic driver tests and
opt-in browser tests (MAESTRO_TEST_BROWSER=true). no new readiness heuristic,
retry loop or fallback is introduced; this deliberately retains the existing
query delay rather than treating every javascript evaluation as safe to rush.
